PN,32603
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F326A1786745069
OL,3,CPotentially deadly livestock virus
OL,4,Cfound in Scotland for first time
OL,6,FThe bluetongue virus primarily affects
OL,7,Fsheep, cattle and goats and is mainly
OL,8,Fspread through biting midges.
OL,10,FSigns of the virus include nasal
OL,11,Fdischarge, redness and swelling of the
OL,12,Flips, nose and muzzle, lameness or
OL,13,Freluctance to stand, decreased milk
OL,14,Fproduction and diarrhoea in cattle.
OL,16,FIt does not affect people or food
OL,17,Fsafety.
OL,1,W{$~k4{$k4~sjw=                 G3/5
OL,2,W/.!+.!/*%/.!+,*%/T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
